Hi,

I m using some R fuctionality with renjin. Witch workes fine when I do it the first time. When I try analyse the second data set. I get the following Error:

Exception in thread "AWT-EventQueue-0" org.renjin.eval.EvalException: object 'price' not found

The code is the same as before:

R_code = "price <- c( 1.199, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, 1.239, ..., 1.239)";
engine.eval(R_code);

Tried allready to delete the object with: engine.eval("rm(price)");
... and "empty" the "old" manager with

ScriptEngineManager manager = null;
manager = new ScriptEngineManager();

Please help.

Best regards,

Georg

